<title>ROMANIA: Romania posts March trade surplus of $33.9 mln.</title>
<headline>Romania posts March trade surplus of $33.9 mln.</headline>
<dateline>BUCHAREST 1997-05-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Romania posted a $33.9 million trade surplus in March, recovering from $51.9 million deficit the previous month, helped by a 6.8 percent drop in imports, National Statistic Board (CNS) data showed.</p>
<p>This was the first monthly trade surplus since September.</p>
<p> ROMANIAN TRADE	 MARCH 97   FEB 97	  MARCH 96</p>
<p> Exports million USD    678.7   639.9 (606.1)    n.a. (606.0)</p>
<p> Imports		    644.8   691.8 (635.2)    n.a. (706.0)</p>
<p> Balance		    +33.9   -51.9 (-29.1)    n.a (-100.0)</p>
<p>(JANUARY TO MONTH)</p>
<p> Exports million USD  1,923.6    n.a. (1,208.9) n.a (1,476.0)</p>
<p> Imports		  2,108.2    n.a. (1,392.2) n.a (1,490.0)</p>
<p> Balance		   -184.6    n.a. (-183.3)  n.a   (-14.0)</p>
<p>NOTES -- Previous data in brackets. All figures in FOB prices and subject to revisions.</p>
<p>Textiles and steel products topped the list of three-month exports.</p>
<p>-- Bucharest Newsroom 40-1 3120264</p>
</text>
